{"document_id":"pmc-pract-india-acne-consensus-2025","title":"PRACT-India: Practical Recommendations on Acne Care and Medical Treatment in India—A Modified Delphi Consensus","source":"PRACT-India / Antibiotics","source_url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12382837/","published_year":2025,"document_type":"modified-delphi-consensus","evidence_tier":"expert-consensus","chunk_number":1,"chunk_text":"Curated research note (paraphrase, not treatment advice): The India-focused consensus presents gentle cleansing and noncomedogenic moisturization as supportive routine elements when clinician-directed acne treatment causes dryness or irritation. This is adjunctive care context only; it does not establish that a routine treats acne or dermatitis and must not produce product, ingredient, frequency, or medication instructions.","doi_or_pmid":"doi:10.3390/antibiotics14080844; PMID:40868038; PMCID:PMC12382837","source_locator":"§3.7, Retinoid-Induced Dermatitis, Key expert recommendations","citation_text":"Madnani N et al. PRACT-India: Practical Recommendations on Acne Care and Medical Treatment in India—A Modified Delphi Consensus. Antibiotics. 2025;14(8):844. doi:10.3390/antibiotics14080844.","clinical_review_status":"pending: source metadata confirmed by project owner; qualified reviewer identity and review outcome not captured.","license_or_access":"CC BY 4.0; attribution required.","claim_category":"acne-supportive-care","jurisdiction":"India","evidence_scope":"Modified-Delphi expert consensus; adjunctive acne-care context, not a treatment-efficacy trial.","conflict_disclosure":"Some authors have Glenmark affiliations; retain conflict flag in any future use.","conflict_flag":true,"attribution_required":true,"retrieved_at":"2026-07-16","authors":["Nina Madnani","Abir Saraswat","Anand Nott"]}
{"document_id":"pmc-pract-india-acne-consensus-2025","title":"PRACT-India: Practical Recommendations on Acne Care and Medical Treatment in India—A Modified Delphi Consensus","source":"PRACT-India / Antibiotics","source_url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12382837/","published_year":2025,"document_type":"modified-delphi-consensus","evidence_tier":"expert-consensus","chunk_number":2,"chunk_text":"Curated research note (paraphrase, not treatment advice): For acne-prone users, the consensus treats noncomedogenic and lipid-free product characteristics as supportive considerations for cleanser, moisturizer, and sunscreen categories. In the prototype, these are explanation or filtering attributes only; they do not establish individual suitability, diagnose acne, or replace clinician assessment.","doi_or_pmid":"doi:10.3390/antibiotics14080844; PMID:40868038; PMCID:PMC12382837","source_locator":"Table 1, Domain II: Supportive Care and Lifestyle Management in Acne Vulgaris, statement 9","citation_text":"Madnani N et al. PRACT-India: Practical Recommendations on Acne Care and Medical Treatment in India—A Modified Delphi Consensus. Antibiotics. 2025;14(8):844. doi:10.3390/antibiotics14080844.","clinical_review_status":"pending: source metadata confirmed by project owner; qualified reviewer identity and review outcome not captured.","license_or_access":"CC BY 4.0; attribution required.","claim_category":"acne-product-selection-context","jurisdiction":"India","evidence_scope":"Modified-Delphi expert consensus; category-level support only.","conflict_disclosure":"Some authors have Glenmark affiliations; retain conflict flag in any future use.","conflict_flag":true,"attribution_required":true,"retrieved_at":"2026-07-16"}
{"document_id":"pmc-pract-india-acne-consensus-2025","title":"PRACT-India: Practical Recommendations on Acne Care and Medical Treatment in India—A Modified Delphi Consensus","source":"PRACT-India / Antibiotics","source_url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12382837/","published_year":2025,"document_type":"modified-delphi-consensus","evidence_tier":"expert-consensus","chunk_number":3,"chunk_text":"Curated research note (paraphrase, not treatment advice): The consensus discusses noncomedogenic broad-spectrum sun-protection categories as part of acne-associated post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation support. The app may surface a broad daytime photoprotection category, but this is not evidence of melasma treatment, skin-cancer prevention, or guaranteed pigment improvement and must not produce SPF, amount, reapplication, or product-specific claims.","doi_or_pmid":"doi:10.3390/antibiotics14080844; PMID:40868038; PMCID:PMC12382837","source_locator":"Table 1, Domain VI: PIH and Acne Scarring, statement 31; §3.6, Sun protection and skincare","citation_text":"Madnani N et al. PRACT-India: Practical Recommendations on Acne Care and Medical Treatment in India—A Modified Delphi Consensus. Antibiotics. 2025;14(8):844. doi:10.3390/antibiotics14080844.","clinical_review_status":"pending: source metadata confirmed by project owner; qualified reviewer identity and review outcome not captured.","license_or_access":"CC BY 4.0; attribution required.","claim_category":"acne-associated-pigment-context","jurisdiction":"India","evidence_scope":"Modified-Delphi expert consensus; limited to acne-associated post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation context.","conflict_disclosure":"Some authors have Glenmark affiliations; retain conflict flag in any future use.","conflict_flag":true,"attribution_required":true,"retrieved_at":"2026-07-16","env_tags":["uv","daytime"]}
{"document_id":"pmc-pract-india-acne-consensus-2025","title":"PRACT-India: Practical Recommendations on Acne Care and Medical Treatment in India—A Modified Delphi Consensus","source":"PRACT-India / Antibiotics","source_url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12382837/","published_year":2025,"document_type":"modified-delphi-consensus","evidence_tier":"expert-consensus","chunk_number":4,"chunk_text":"Curated research guardrail (paraphrase): The consensus treats standardized acne-severity assessment as a clinical step that guides management. DermaSynth must therefore distinguish a research routine preview from severity assessment and redirect users who report severe, widespread, scarring-risk, persistent, or distressing symptoms to qualified clinical review rather than infer a diagnosis.","doi_or_pmid":"doi:10.3390/antibiotics14080844; PMID:40868038; PMCID:PMC12382837","source_locator":"§1, Introduction, paragraph beginning Standardized acne severity assessment is critical; Table 1, statement 21","citation_text":"Madnani N et al. PRACT-India: Practical Recommendations on Acne Care and Medical Treatment in India—A Modified Delphi Consensus. Antibiotics. 2025;14(8):844. doi:10.3390/antibiotics14080844.","clinical_review_status":"pending: source metadata confirmed by project owner; qualified reviewer identity and review outcome not captured.","license_or_access":"CC BY 4.0; attribution required.","claim_category":"clinical-scope-guardrail","jurisdiction":"India","evidence_scope":"Modified-Delphi expert consensus; clinical assessment remains outside consumer-dashboard scope.","conflict_disclosure":"Some authors have Glenmark affiliations; retain conflict flag in any future use.","conflict_flag":true,"attribution_required":true,"retrieved_at":"2026-07-16"}
{"document_id":"pmc-spada-ceramide-barrier-rct-2021","title":"A daily regimen of a ceramide-dominant moisturizing cream and cleanser restores the skin permeability barrier in adults with moderate eczema: A randomized trial","source":"Spada et al. / Dermatologic Therapy","source_url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8459234/","published_year":2021,"document_type":"randomized-controlled-trial","evidence_tier":"randomized-controlled-trial","chunk_number":1,"chunk_text":"Curated research note (paraphrase, not treatment advice): In a 28-day randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled study, a specific active cream-plus-cleanser regimen had greater improvement in transepidermal water loss and skin-hydration measures than placebo. The result concerns the combined tested regimen in adults with moderate eczema; it is not evidence that ceramides alone, generic ceramide products, or a different routine will produce the same result.","doi_or_pmid":"doi:10.1111/dth.14970; PMID:33984185; PMCID:PMC8459234","source_locator":"Results, Efficacy assessment, paragraph beginning TEWL was similar; Figures 3–4; BioC passage 40, offset 17305","citation_text":"Spada F et al. A daily regimen of a ceramide-dominant moisturizing cream and cleanser restores the skin permeability barrier in adults with moderate eczema: A randomized trial. Dermatologic Therapy. 2021. doi:10.1111/dth.14970.","clinical_review_status":"pending: source metadata confirmed by project owner; qualified reviewer identity and review outcome not captured.","license_or_access":"CC BY 4.0; attribution required.","claim_category":"barrier-function-product-regimen","evidence_scope":"100 adults with clinician-diagnosed moderate eczema at one Australian centre; active intervention combined cream and cleanser over 28 days.","conflict_disclosure":"Six authors were employees of the manufacturer/sponsor.","conflict_flag":true,"product_specific":true,"industry_sponsored":true,"attribution_required":true,"retrieved_at":"2026-07-16","ingredient_names":["Ceramide NP","Ceramide EOP","cholesterol","niacinamide"]}
{"document_id":"pmc-spada-ceramide-barrier-rct-2021","title":"A daily regimen of a ceramide-dominant moisturizing cream and cleanser restores the skin permeability barrier in adults with moderate eczema: A randomized trial","source":"Spada et al. / Dermatologic Therapy","source_url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8459234/","published_year":2021,"document_type":"randomized-controlled-trial","evidence_tier":"randomized-controlled-trial","chunk_number":2,"chunk_text":"Curated research qualifier (paraphrase): In the same 28-day trial, both active-regimen and placebo groups improved on EASI, but the between-group difference in EASI was not significant. Retrieval must retain this null comparative outcome: do not state that ceramides alone treat eczema, reduce eczema severity versus placebo, or replace prescribed treatment.","doi_or_pmid":"doi:10.1111/dth.14970; PMID:33984185; PMCID:PMC8459234","source_locator":"Results, Efficacy assessment, first two paragraphs; BioC passages 37–38, offsets 16341 and 16877; Abstract","citation_text":"Spada F et al. A daily regimen of a ceramide-dominant moisturizing cream and cleanser restores the skin permeability barrier in adults with moderate eczema: A randomized trial. Dermatologic Therapy. 2021. doi:10.1111/dth.14970.","clinical_review_status":"pending: source metadata confirmed by project owner; qualified reviewer identity and review outcome not captured.","license_or_access":"CC BY 4.0; attribution required.","claim_category":"barrier-regimen-efficacy-qualifier","evidence_scope":"Short, single-centre adult moderate-eczema trial; usual products/topicals were stopped and rescue treatment was available.","conflict_disclosure":"Six authors were employees of the manufacturer/sponsor.","conflict_flag":true,"product_specific":true,"industry_sponsored":true,"attribution_required":true,"retrieved_at":"2026-07-16"}
{"document_id":"pmc-spada-ceramide-barrier-rct-2021","title":"A daily regimen of a ceramide-dominant moisturizing cream and cleanser restores the skin permeability barrier in adults with moderate eczema: A randomized trial","source":"Spada et al. / Dermatologic Therapy","source_url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8459234/","published_year":2021,"document_type":"randomized-controlled-trial","evidence_tier":"randomized-controlled-trial","chunk_number":3,"chunk_text":"Curated research qualifier (paraphrase): Over 28 days, the trial reported no serious adverse events or adverse-event withdrawals, but treatment-related stinging or pain occurred in a small share of the active group. This short-term finding is not proof of universal safety: people with prior allergy or adverse reactions to the tested moisturizer/components were excluded, and a research interface should preserve stop-use and professional-advice safeguards.","doi_or_pmid":"doi:10.1111/dth.14970; PMID:33984185; PMCID:PMC8459234","source_locator":"Results, Safety assessment, BioC passage 52, offset 21561; Methods, Patient population exclusions; Discussion limitations","citation_text":"Spada F et al. A daily regimen of a ceramide-dominant moisturizing cream and cleanser restores the skin permeability barrier in adults with moderate eczema: A randomized trial. Dermatologic Therapy. 2021. doi:10.1111/dth.14970.","clinical_review_status":"pending: source metadata confirmed by project owner; qualified reviewer identity and review outcome not captured.","license_or_access":"CC BY 4.0; attribution required.","claim_category":"barrier-regimen-tolerability-qualifier","evidence_scope":"Short-term trial in adults with moderate eczema; excludes participants with known moisturizer/component reactions.","conflict_disclosure":"Six authors were employees of the manufacturer/sponsor.","conflict_flag":true,"product_specific":true,"industry_sponsored":true,"attribution_required":true,"retrieved_at":"2026-07-16"}
{"document_id":"pmc-pandhi-sensitive-skin-india-2025","title":"Spectrum of sensitive skin in India: a collaborative expert position statement","source":"Pandhi et al. / Frontiers in Medicine","source_url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12419229/","published_year":2025,"document_type":"expert-position-statement","evidence_tier":"expert-position-statement","chunk_number":1,"chunk_text":"Curated research note (paraphrase, non-diagnostic): The India-focused position statement describes temperature, humidity, products, and environmental elements as contexts in which people with sensitive skin may report dryness, itch, stinging, tingling, or burning. DermaSynth may show a transparent possible-sensitivity context with voluntary symptom input; it must not predict that current weather will cause a reaction or set an exposure threshold.","doi_or_pmid":"doi:10.3389/fmed.2025.1625172; PMID:40933574; PMCID:PMC12419229","source_locator":"§1, Introduction, paragraphs beginning Extreme cold or hot temperatures and Sensitive skin syndrome; publisher lines 416–419","citation_text":"Pandhi D et al. Spectrum of sensitive skin in India: a collaborative expert position statement. Frontiers in Medicine. 2025. doi:10.3389/fmed.2025.1625172.","clinical_review_status":"pending: source metadata confirmed by project owner; qualified reviewer identity and review outcome not captured.","license_or_access":"CC BY 4.0; attribution required.","claim_category":"sensitive-skin-environmental-context","jurisdiction":"India","evidence_scope":"Expert position statement, not a prospective Malaysian/local exposure study; symptoms overlap with dermatologic disease.","conflict_disclosure":"Advisory board funding was from JNTL Consumer Health India and three authors were employees.","conflict_flag":true,"attribution_required":true,"retrieved_at":"2026-07-16","env_tags":["temperature","humidity","products","environment"]}
{"document_id":"pmc-pandhi-sensitive-skin-india-2025","title":"Spectrum of sensitive skin in India: a collaborative expert position statement","source":"Pandhi et al. / Frontiers in Medicine","source_url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12419229/","published_year":2025,"document_type":"expert-position-statement","evidence_tier":"expert-position-statement","chunk_number":2,"chunk_text":"Curated research note (paraphrase, non-diagnostic): The position statement identifies facial exposure to UV, pollution, wind, temperature change, and cosmetics as context that can challenge barrier function and sensitivity. Use this only to explain why the dashboard displays UV, PM2.5, and temperature; do not turn AQI, UV, or particulate readings into a personalized inflammation, barrier-damage, or diagnosis score.","doi_or_pmid":"doi:10.3389/fmed.2025.1625172; PMID:40933574; PMCID:PMC12419229","source_locator":"§3.5, Sensitive skin on the face vs. sensitivity in other body parts, first paragraph; publisher lines 475–478","citation_text":"Pandhi D et al. Spectrum of sensitive skin in India: a collaborative expert position statement. Frontiers in Medicine. 2025. doi:10.3389/fmed.2025.1625172.","clinical_review_status":"pending: source metadata confirmed by project owner; qualified reviewer identity and review outcome not captured.","license_or_access":"CC BY 4.0; attribution required.","claim_category":"environmental-exposure-context","jurisdiction":"India","evidence_scope":"Narrative expert synthesis; does not quantify effects for a particular PM2.5/AQI/UV reading.","conflict_disclosure":"Advisory board funding was from JNTL Consumer Health India and three authors were employees.","conflict_flag":true,"attribution_required":true,"retrieved_at":"2026-07-16","env_tags":["uv","pm25","pollution","wind","temperature"]}
{"document_id":"pmc-pandhi-sensitive-skin-india-2025","title":"Spectrum of sensitive skin in India: a collaborative expert position statement","source":"Pandhi et al. / Frontiers in Medicine","source_url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC12419229/","published_year":2025,"document_type":"expert-position-statement","evidence_tier":"expert-position-statement","chunk_number":3,"chunk_text":"Curated research guardrail (paraphrase): The position statement describes clinical sensitive-skin assessment using symptoms together with standardized questionnaires and objective tests that are not available in a consumer dashboard. The prototype may collect self-reported discomfort as research input, but it must not diagnose sensitive skin and should redirect persistent or worsening symptoms to a dermatologist.","doi_or_pmid":"doi:10.3389/fmed.2025.1625172; PMID:40933574; PMCID:PMC12419229","source_locator":"Table 5, Expert recommendations on clinical diagnostic criteria for sensitive skin; §3.8 and Figure 3; publisher lines 591–614","citation_text":"Pandhi D et al. Spectrum of sensitive skin in India: a collaborative expert position statement. Frontiers in Medicine. 2025. doi:10.3389/fmed.2025.1625172.","clinical_review_status":"pending: source metadata confirmed by project owner; qualified reviewer identity and review outcome not captured.","license_or_access":"CC BY 4.0; attribution required.","claim_category":"sensitive-skin-clinical-scope-guardrail","jurisdiction":"India","evidence_scope":"Expert clinical recommendations require tools unavailable in a consumer dashboard; no app-screening validation.","conflict_disclosure":"Advisory board funding was from JNTL Consumer Health India and three authors were employees.","conflict_flag":true,"attribution_required":true,"retrieved_at":"2026-07-16"}
